  the point did you know that you can cut  off his arm preemptively just put  yourself in a more risky position to  focus your attacks on it and it'll fall  off once you've dealt about 50% of his  maximum health to his arm exclusively  which makes the whole process pretty  redundant really your time is better  spent hitting one leg and then dashing  to the other anyway discovering this one  fact made me pretty sad actually because  I know that if this was dark souls 1 I  would have got a weapon out of that 7  let's move on to the pit the first point  I want to talk about is something I read  in the comments of my pit  video cheers - Kotori gays Joker for  tipping me off on this one so he said  that there was a zip line hidden in the  gutter and I was like what I thought I'd  been completely thorough when I explored  the gutter but after a lot of searching  I eventually followed the zip line cable  above and found out where to access it  so after that first exploding undead on  the bridge you should continue along in  that direction until you find this  corner drop-off explore climb up and  eventually you'll find these items and a  zip line that allows you to skip what is  essentially half of Blighttown 2.0 I  could not believe this existed I thought  who knew it all I'm going to leave a  dislike on my video out of shame moving  on to something else I missed in the  gutter number eight  you know those sconces that you can  light in this area I didn't notice it  before but they're essentially  repurposed statues with their heads cut  off the body has lost its form but at  the base of each one is the severed head  of a statue with number nine and ten we  move on to areas that I'm not planning  on having full episodes on because they  only have about one or two hidden things  within them so first up at number nine  is dead man's Wharf you call the pirate  ship in by ringing a bell but did you  know that you can bypass a chunk of the  stage by shooting an arrow at this bell  instead you can essentially bring the  ship in from across the map with an iron  arrow I set off the bell which rings to  bring the ship in early that's a pretty  neat little detail and finally I debated  including the dark chasm in my pit video  but ultimately I decided against it  there's this one neat fact in this place  though and it's in the dark chasm of  drangleic castle when you go down there  you can peek through the stone here at  the end of the stage and you can see the  best boss in the game waiting for you on  the other side and honestly I kind of  just included this fact so that I could  talk about this boss so dark loka is an  optional boss you get from exploring all  three dark chasms and he's got to be the  best boss fight in the game hasn't he  this was my first time fighting him and  it's one of those fights where you can  just marvel at the design so it starts  off it's just you and one dark lager he  has a melee combo an AoE self explosion  for ranged methods of attack I think and  also a teleport  now the thing about his attacks is  they're all incredibly easy to predict  firstly each one is a different color  with a melee combo he takes a moment to  conjure the bright spell sword and it  also uses a combo that can be really  easily dodged by pretty much just  spamming the Dodge button in regards to  his ranged attacks he conjures three  colored spheres and all of these hover  above his head for a few seconds before  firing which allows you to take in  what's about to happen  one is fire shooting a series of  explosive fireballs in quick succession  another is a dark spell he'll conjure  two dark portals and should a dark orb  into one which will fly out of the other  towards you which will explode and knock  you off your feet upon nearby impact  with the ground he can also signal for a  type of light purple soul arrow to fly  at you from his hands his fourth attack  is a purple laser something that will  start off slow but track your movement  and force you to run and keep away so  since you can predict all this it's  gonna be pretty easy right wrong these  were only easy in order to train you for  what's about to come now that you've  been given ample time to memorize the  visual cues dark lager splits in two you  now have to deal with a flurry of  attacks that threaten to overwhelm you  but these are attacks that are really  predictable and in an arena that's quite  manageable it's a fight where you have  to manage your camera well but also one  where you're forced to anticipate two  opponents they've done a brilliant job  of balancing the speeds and the timing  of his attacks it feels like you're  performing this intricate dance every  time you fight for example you might  know that one of these fireballs is  about to fire so you need to run the  perfect amount of distance to put you  into striking distance of the other dark  loka is one firing a laser I should try  and run underneath him at an angle where  I can keep both in my camera so you know  these are the things that you're  thinking you're constantly in this  ongoing focused state of mind now  compare this to another duel fight that  I hate the throne defender and watcher  so in this fight you're constantly  backpedaling waiting for both enemies to  attack at once just so they'll both be  open and in my opinion this is just  shitty boss design it's not fun or  satisfying to fight that way and their  attacks aren't  which means you're actually forced to  backpedal if you could predict their  attacks it would still be hard because  there's two of them but at least you  could get in the thick of it and cut  them down by anticipating movements but  in the present form of the fight you  can't you just have to play this waiting  game where you backpedal and wait for an  opening or you can make the fight  completely trivial by summoning helpers  splitting their attention with dark Luka  you can anticipate slow paced ranged  attacks and plan accordingly with your  movements meaning mistakes are  completely your own with the thrown  rumors you're forced to backpedal and  stay on the edge of their attacks and  god forbid you actually try to heal  because they can launch attacks with  unpredictable warning meaning that way  you survive one time you may not survive  another you know the souls games are at  their best when damage is not left to  chance it should be left to your ability  to predict and anticipate bear in mind  I'm not complaining that the fight is  too hot I'm not it's just bringing out  the worst of the souls combat system  whereas the dark look of fight brings  out the best I do love the fact that you  have to take out the watcher and  defender evenly though that's a nice  touch and it's something that I just  wish was realized within better combat  design so dark lock is an awesome boss  you should check it out and also check  out the other 10 things episodes if you  missed them they're a lot of fun to  produce and share with you guys  oh yeah and soon we should have another  soul song ready to go so get hype and  I'll see you in the next one  later guys and thanks for supporting the  channel

